<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry the Fowler</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 876–936</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Henry I of Germany, Henry the Fowler of Saxony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry the Fowler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a>, was elected king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a> in 919, the first of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottonian-dynasty">Ottonian dynasty</a>. He won over the dukes of Swabia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, regained Lotharingia, campaigned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> from the Hevelli, and defeated the Hungarians at Riade in 933. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-i">Otto I</a> became emperor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler.jpg" alt="Henry the Fowler" width="315" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siegel_Heinrich_I_Posse.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
